  "id": "fuzzy-trace-theory",
  "term": "fuzzy trace theory",
  "definition": "Fuzzy trace theory is a memory theory proposing that people store two kinds of traces from experience: a detailed, item-specific trace and a more general trace of the meaning. It is used to explain false memories by suggesting that people may later rely on the meaning-based trace, which tends to last longer than the detailed trace.",
